course: dictionary
lesson: 9646
title: Stylish: looking good and doing it well
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Stylish» is an adjective, so it describes a thing or a person. It has two meanings. The first is fashionable and good-looking, in a smart, attractive way: «a stylish jacket». The second is done with skill and grace: «a stylish goal» is a goal scored in a graceful, skilful way.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. «In London, Kwesi's uncle comes from Ghana for a wedding wearing kente, a bright woven cloth.» The wedding and the bright cloth show he looks smart. Kwesi's mates say «Your uncle's drip is crazy», and drip is slang for stylish clothes, so their praise fits the first meaning.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «She wore a stylish dress to the party» still makes sense with stylish meaning fashionable. Stylish is more than pretty: it tells you something has a smart, polished look or that someone moves or plays with grace.
fact: «Stylish» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in «a stylish design».
fact: «Stylish» means fashionable and good-looking, in a smart, attractive way.
fact: «Stylish» can also mean done with skill and grace, in a way that looks good: «a stylish goal».
fact: «Drip» is slang for stylish clothes: «Your uncle's drip is crazy» means his outfit looks amazing.
fact: Useful phrases are «stylish clothes», «a stylish design» and «look stylish».
exercise: What does «stylish» mean? | Cold and wet | *Fashionable and good-looking | Very old and dusty | Loud and noisy
exercise: «The striker scored a stylish goal in the last minute.» What does stylish describe here? | A goal that was not allowed | A goal that was very slow | A goal that was scored by accident | *A goal done with skill and grace
exercise: Kwesi's mates say «Your uncle's drip is crazy». What does drip mean? | *Stylish clothes | A leaking tap | Sad and tired | A wet, grey day
test: «The architect's stylish design won the prize.» What does stylish mean here? | *Fashionable and smart, with a graceful look | Old and falling apart | Grey and rainy | Noisy and crowded
test: Which phrase uses stylish correctly? | the stylish rained | stylish quickly ran | stylish to the table | *a stylish design
exam: Jayden says «Stylish is just another word for pretty.» Is he right? | *No, stylish can mean fashionable and smart, or done with skill and grace | Yes, and it is always about the weather | Yes, the two words mean exactly the same | No, stylish means old
